              <subject>https://w3id.org/italia/work-accident/onto/risk_management/Perito</subject>
              <property>http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label</property>
              <object>
                <lexicalForm>Perito</lexicalForm>
                <datatype/>
                <language>it</language>
              </object>
            </annotation>
            <annotation>
              <subject>https://w3id.org/italia/work-accident/onto/risk_management/Perito</subject>
              <property>http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment</property>
              <object>
                <lexicalForm>Esperto incaricato di un'indagine tecnica (perizia) per conto di privati, sia per incarico del giudice, cui riferisce mediante dichiarazione giurata. Il giudice interviene solo se c'è un ricorso e si arriva in giudizio. In tal caso il giudice può nominare un secondo perito per capire se il progetto di prevenzione può beneficiare o meno al finanziamento.</lexicalForm>
                <datatype/>
                <language>it</language>
              </object>
            </annotation>
            <annotation>
              <subject>https://w3id.org/italia/work-accident/onto/risk_management/Perito</subject>
              <property>http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label</property>
              <object>
                <lexicalForm>Quantity Surveyor</lexicalForm>
                <datatype/>
                <language>en</language>
              </object>
            </annotation>
            <annotation>
              <subject>https://w3id.org/italia/work-accident/onto/risk_management/Perito</subject>
              <property>http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment</property>
              <object>
                <lexicalForm>An expert whose main role is to carry out a survey on behalf of either a private client or a judge. The latter, usually gets involved in the inspection process, only in case of an appeall or final examination. A judge can decide to appoint a second Quantity Surveyor to help them decide if the assesed plan can potentially qualify for the INAIL managemnt risk funding program.</lexicalForm>
                <datatype/>
                <language>en</language>
              </object>
            </annotation>
          </annotations>
        </iri>
